  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Saving Lives Through Anticipatory Action: Cyclone Preparedness and Response in Mozambique</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Communities in Mozambique face recurring cyclones that damage homes, displace families, and disrupt access to essential services. This project is strengthening preparedness and providing early assistance to people living in the most cyclone affected provinces, including Cabo Delgado, Nampula, Zamb&#xe9;zia, Sofala, Inhambane, and Gaza. The project supports families by supplying emergency shelter materials and essential household items that help them protect themselves before and after a cyclone. Temporary accommodation centres are being assessed and prepared so they can safely host people who may need to evacuate. At risk communities will receive clear early warning messages to help them take timely action during severe weather events. Through these planned efforts, the project is strengthening local preparedness, improving the safety and dignity of people who may become displaced, and supporting a more coordinated and timely emergency response to the growing risks posed by recurrent cyclones in Mozambique.</narrative>
  </description>
